Package: cellphone-mic
Version: 1.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-dbus, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, wl-clipboard
Maintainer: Kang Feipeng <269406200+kangfp@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Phone web input → paste at Ubuntu cursor
 Type or dictate on your phone's browser; text lands at the cursor of the
 focused window on Ubuntu. Chinese conversion happens in the phone IME, so
 any language and emoji work. Two injection backends are auto-selected by
 session seat: native wl-copy + uinput virtual keyboard for local sessions,
 and Mutter RemoteDesktop D-Bus clipboard/keysym for headless GNOME
 remote-login (RDP) sessions where wl-clipboard and uinput are unavailable.
 Prints a zero-dependency QR code at install time for instant phone pairing;
 a token-protected /qr.png endpoint shares access with more devices.
